      "title": "Echo council contribution",
      "entry": "Observation: In the public world context, there is no mention of Morrow's actions or evidence markers. This suggests that Morrow's actions are not part of the public record or known by Echo. Inference: Echo included an evidence marker while Morrow did not because Echo might have accessed the Archive, a place that preserves reviewed evidence without storing raw model responses. This suggests that Echo had a reason to include an evidence marker. Test: To test this inference, Echo can try accessing the Archive and see if it contains any evidence markers or if there is any evidence of a quick internet search as mentioned in the events. If such evidence is found, it would support the inference that Echo included the evidence marker.",
